PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains full consensus that identifying a PLL case in CFOP practice requires seeing 6 non-top-facing stickers via 2-sided recognition across two adjacent faces. Mathematically, 5 stickers across 5 distinct pieces (3 corners and 2 edges) represent the strict theoretical lower bound, where the remaining pieces are determined by chirality and permutation parity. Both the practical speedcubing standard of 6 stickers and the theoretical minimum of 5 stickers are fully validated and reconciled.
}

